{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>For.</b> The meaning: you have reason to spare him." "<b>And the meaning of 'for I am gracious' (כי חנון אני).</b> According to the Gaon [Saadia] it is like חנני חנני (Job 19:21), and the meaning is: for I will give him wealth and remove what is yours. But in my opinion the word חנינה is not so, for what would David ask to say חנני אלהים כחסדך (Psalms 51:3) — only it is like 'merciful,' although there is a difference between them, as I will explain in [the pericope] Ki Tissa." "Now this, 'and I will hear' — it follows after 'and it shall be when he cries out to Me,' like what is written above: כי אם צעק יצעק אלי שמע אשמע צעקתו, and 'My anger will burn' — and how will it be known that 'I will indeed hear his cry'? By 'the burning of My anger' that comes after it."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:29.977605642Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}